     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks, Richard.  That has saved me a lot of time.  Yes, I&#39;m out of luck.  The text output file from <font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>dput </b></font>gives me all of the info I need so I&#39;ll just grab things from there.  (Why do I want to use something like <font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>dput</b></font>?  I have data/models that take hours and all can&#39;t be run sequentially without rebooting my computer.  I&#39;ve tried &quot;<font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>save</b></font>&quot; and &quot;<font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>saveRDS</b></font>&quot; but those approaches make huge files that are hard to transport.)<div><br></div><div>Jim</div></div>"
